{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.constant_curvature","record":{"id":"scalar.constant_curvature","kind":"claim","label":"Separate positive and zero constant-interval inequalities","status":"unverified","source_id":"support_tex_curvature","locator":"curvature.tex:9–52; prop:gap-curvature; regularity.tex:240–308","statement":"For gamma∈U constant c on an open interval I⊂(0,1), q(t)=E Phi_x(t,X_t)². If c>0 then q‴(t)≥(1000 c²)^(−1) E[(c Phi_xx(t,X_t))⁴]>0 for every t∈I, so q′ is strictly convex. If c=0 then q′ is strictly increasing, by q″=E Phi_xxx²>0.","assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_admissible"],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-constant-curvature"],"boundary":"Minimality is not used. Approximation transfers only bounded derivative moments on a fixed compact strip; no convergence of density scores or their ratios is claimed. The c=0 proof is separate, never division by c."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.constant_curvature","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[],"direct_passages":[]},"aligned_passages":[],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=scalar.constant_curvature&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=scalar.constant_curvature&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=scalar.constant_curvature&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&node=scalar.constant_curvature&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"field:3a15a0724b127b7bfb9552de630a197b50446fd4fdce6147038da619682cd2